@startuml
title 31. Queue-Based Async Sync System

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

participant "Client" as Client
participant "QueueSyncHandler" as Handler
participant "QueueSyncService" as QSvc
participant "PostgreSQL\n(sync_jobs)" as DB
participant "Redis\n(queue + progress)" as Redis
participant "WorkerPool" as Worker
participant "Processor" as Proc
participant "Domain Services" as Domain

== Enqueue Flow ==

Client -> Handler: POST /sync/enqueue/{appID}?type=full_sync
activate Handler
Handler -> QSvc: EnqueueSync(appID, userID, type, priority)
activate QSvc
QSvc -> DB: FindActiveByAppIDAndType() — duplicate check
DB --> QSvc: nil (no duplicate)
QSvc -> DB: INSERT sync_jobs (status=pending)
QSvc -> Redis: LPUSH :queue:full {jobPayload}
QSvc --> Handler: job (with ID)
deactivate QSvc
Handler --> Client: 202 Accepted { job_id }
deactivate Handler

== Worker Processing ==

Worker -> Redis: BRPOP :queue:full (blocking)
Redis --> Worker: jobPayload
activate Worker

note right of Worker: 1. Acquire lock BEFORE marking started\n2. Lock → MarkStarted → heartbeat → process

Worker -> Redis: SETNX lock:appID:type workerID (acquire lock)
Worker -> Redis: SET heartbeat:{jobID} (immediate — prevents steal race)
Worker -> DB: UPDATE status='processing' WHERE status='pending'
Worker -> Worker: Start heartbeat goroutine (ownership-aware)

Worker -> Proc: Process(ctx, payload)
activate Proc

note right of Proc: Execute domain logic\n(returns nil on success, error on failure)

Proc -> Domain: FetchTransactions / RebuildLedger / etc.
activate Domain
Domain --> Proc: results
deactivate Domain

loop every ~2s
  Proc -> Redis: HSET progress:{jobID} completed=N, message="..."
end

Proc --> Worker: nil (success) or error
deactivate Proc

alt success (nil returned)
  Worker -> DB: UPDATE status='completed' WHERE status='processing'
else shutdown (ctx cancelled)
  note right of Worker: Leave in 'processing'\nRecovery re-enqueues on restart
else failure (error returned)
  Worker -> DB: UPDATE status='failed' WHERE status IN ('pending','processing')
end

note right of Worker: Cleanup: ownership-aware lock release

Worker -> Redis: Lua: DEL lock IF value==workerID
Worker -> Redis: DEL heartbeat:{jobID}
deactivate Worker

== Full Sync Orchestration ==

participant "FullSyncProcessor" as FSP

Worker -> FSP: Process(ctx, full_sync_payload)
activate FSP

note right of FSP: Wave 1 — No subscription dependency

FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {transaction_sync}
FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {review_sync}

loop poll until transaction_sync completes (5s)
  FSP -> DB: FindByID(txSyncJobID)
end

note right of FSP: Wave 2 — Depends on subscriptions\n(from ledger rebuild)

FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {event_sync}
FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {status_sync}
FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {store_sync}

note right of FSP: status_sync reconciles each sub's event-derived\nstatus against billing (cancel-trap): a CANCELLED/\nUNINSTALLED churns only when no recurring charge\npost-dates the event; risk is re-derived from charge\nrecency (Subscription.ApplyEventStatus).

loop poll Wave 2 children until done (5s)
  FSP -> DB: FindByParentJobID(parentID)
end

note right of FSP: Wave 3 — AFTER status_sync so the daily snapshot\nreflects the RECONCILED risk (else Dashboard would\nshow pre-reconciliation charge-only risk — RISK-1).

FSP -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {snapshot_sync}

loop poll snapshot child until done (5s)
  FSP -> DB: FindByParentJobID(parentID)
end

note right of FSP: SnapshotProcessor: BackfillHistoricalSnapshots\n(replay txns) then RefreshTodaySnapshot (recompute\ntoday from the current reconciled subscriptions).

FSP --> Worker: nil (or UpdateStatus partial_failure)
deactivate FSP

== Auto-Sync on App Selection ==

participant "AppHandler" as AppH

Client -> AppH: POST /apps/select { partner_app_id, name }
activate AppH
AppH -> DB: appRepo.Create(app)
AppH -> QSvc: TriggerSync(appID, userID, partnerAccountID)
activate QSvc
QSvc -> DB: INSERT sync_jobs (priority=1, type=full_sync)
QSvc -> Redis: LPUSH :queue:full {payload}
QSvc --> AppH: nil (success)
deactivate QSvc
AppH --> Client: 201 Created { sync_triggered: true }
deactivate AppH

== Recovery (Startup) ==

participant "RecoveryService" as Recovery

note over Recovery: Runs on every server boot

Recovery -> DB: Find jobs WHERE status='processing'
Recovery -> Redis: HasHeartbeat(jobID)?

alt no heartbeat (stale)
  alt child job with parent also stale
    Recovery -> DB: MarkFailed("parent recovered")\n(parent will recreate it)
  else standalone or parent job
    Recovery -> Redis: ForceReleaseLock (stale locks)
    Recovery -> DB: MarkPendingIfProcessing (conditional)
    Recovery -> Redis: Re-enqueue to queue
  end
end

note over Recovery: Pending jobs: re-enqueue to Redis only\n(no lock release — they don't hold locks)

== Recovery (Periodic — every 10 min) ==

note over Recovery: Grace: skip started < 2 min ago\nThreshold: started > 2h (lockTTL) AND no heartbeat

Recovery -> DB: Find processing jobs > 2h old
Recovery -> Redis: HasHeartbeat? → if no → re-enqueue

@enduml
